From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: HDR frames get EDR only while they show HDR

What: with the app's HDR switch, a layer that shows a PQ surface has
wantsExtendedDynamicRangeContent off while the guest's frames are SDR,
and on (as before) from the first look that sees HDR, off again 10 s
after the last such look. A look, at most 4 times a second while PQ
frames are drawn, runs the peak shader (ui/omacvm-hdr-tag.h) over the
guest's whole frame on QEMU's present context, two passes into small R32F
targets, and reads the result back through a pixel buffer at a timer 125
ms later. QEMU's thread puts a private SDR flag (OMACVM_HDR_SURF_SDR_KEY)
on each PQ surface whose frame is SDR before Core Animation gets it;
cocoa_gl_layer_follow sets each layer (the main one and every tile layer)
from its own surface's flag (omacvm_hdr_layer). Tone map never for every
PQ or linear surface in both states, set on its own condition. A switch
asks for a whole frame (the partial present's signature), and tile layers
drop EDR when they are hidden. PQ surfaces carry no headroom tag (3.3.0's
first try tagged them 1.0, which macOS ignores). PQ frames start SDR: at
the VM's start, when extra brightness turns off, when the output turns
10-bit, on another display. While SDR, the guest is told the headroom it
had with EDR on, on this display (else the display's most, capped 16),
never the ~1 the panel falls to; after EDR turns on not less than that
until macOS's ramp is done (3 s).
qemu.log: "cocoa: HDR: SDR frames (peak 1.00x), EDR off" and
"cocoa: HDR: HDR frames (peak 4.93x), EDR on".

Why: a layer with EDR on makes macOS raise the panel's headroom to its
most whenever it shows (1.2 -> 14 within 2 s on an M1 Max XDR at
brightness 0.1), also when every pixel is SDR. The user saw "a flash of
full brightness when opening chrome or so, for a split second" with HDR
on and extra brightness off; the guest's frames were measured clean, so
that headroom is the likely cause (not yet seen on screen). With EDR off
for SDR frames the panel stayed at 1.20-1.21 (a probe built like QEMU's
layer, macOS 27.0.1: white window opens, cover and uncover); HDR reached
4x in 0.92 s; SDR white read 1.000 in SDR, HDR and SDR again.
macOS keeps the panel high for about 15 s after the last EDR frame
whatever the layer does; the 10 s hold stays (fewer ramps in videos
with dark scenes). The first frames of new HDR content (up to about 0.4
s, the look and its read back) show clipped at SDR white.

macOS 26 and later only: macOS 15 keeps EDR on for every PQ frame as in
3.2.22 (EDR off with tone map never was not checked there; if 15 maps PQ
again, SDR white would be half). OMACVM_HDR_SDR_TAG=0 does the same.

Threads: QEMU's thread (BQL) owns the look, its timer and the flags (set
before a surface goes to Core Animation); the commit threads read a
surface's flag; the main thread reads the SDR state for the guest's
headroom and counts a new display (qatomic).

OMACVM_HDR_TRACE=1 (tests): a look at every frame and one qemu.log line
per frame (its peak), per layer it goes on (its commit's number, the
surface's SDR flag, EDR, tone map, headroom, format, colour space and
tag) and per tile layer hidden.

Upstream: OmacVM only (IOSurface present).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-hdr-sdr-tag.sh (rules, shader,
wiring; --self-test: the wiring checks fail on 3.3.0's cocoa.m).
Applies before omacvm-cocoa-no-app-nap.patch (the last cocoa patch), after
omacvm-cocoa-drop.patch and omacvm-cocoa-hdr-sdr-tag-logic.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@
 #include "ui/omacvm-modifiers.h"
 #include "ui/omacvm-display-settle.h"
 #include "ui/omacvm-edr.h"
+#include "ui/omacvm-hdr-tag.h"
 #include "ui/omacvm-bright.h"
 #include "ui/omacvm-pointer-bright.h"
 #include "ui/omacvm-pointer-heads.h"
@@ -9455,9 +9456,464 @@
     return CGColorSpaceCreateWithName(deep && cocoa_gl_present_hdr_wanted() ?
                                       kCGColorSpaceITUR_2100_PQ :
                                       kCGColorSpaceSRGB);
+}
+
+/*
+ * OmacVM, HDR (ADR 0049, amended; ui/omacvm-hdr-tag.h): EDR only while
+ * PQ frames show HDR. A layer with EDR on made macOS raise an XDR panel's
+ * headroom to its most (up to 16) whenever the VM showed, also for
+ * SDR-only frames; that is the likely cause of a short full-brightness
+ * flash as a white window opened. A headroom tag of 1.0 on the surface
+ * does not stop it (macOS ignores exactly 1.0; 3.3.0's first try). Now a
+ * look at most 4 times a second takes the frame's brightest value (the peak
+ * shader, two passes on present_ctx, read back through a buffer at the next
+ * timer). While it is SDR white or less each PQ surface carries a private
+ * SDR flag (OMACVM_HDR_SURF_SDR_KEY) and its layer has EDR off; from the
+ * first look that sees more the flag goes and EDR is on, as before; off
+ * again 10 s after the last such look. Tone map never for every PQ or
+ * linear surface in both states, else macOS maps PQ again with EDR off and
+ * SDR white drops to half. Each layer follows its own surface's flag (the
+ * main layer and every tile layer alike), so a switch also asks for a whole
+ * frame (the partial present's signature), and hidden tile layers drop EDR.
+ *
+ * Threads: QEMU's thread (BQL) owns omacvm_hdr (the look, its timer, the
+ * flags, set before a surface goes to Core Animation); the commit threads
+ * read a surface's flag in cocoa_gl_layer_follow; the main thread reads
+ * omacvm_hdr_need_c and omacvm_hdr_open_ns for the guest's headroom
+ * (omacvm_edr_now) and counts a new display in omacvm_hdr_display_gen.
+ * macOS 26 and later only (omacvm_hdr_rule_on); macOS 15 and
+ * OMACVM_HDR_SDR_TAG=0: EDR on for every PQ frame, as in 3.2.22.
+ * OMACVM_HDR_TRACE=1 (tests): a look at every frame, and a qemu.log line
+ * per frame, per layer it goes on and per tile layer hidden, each with its
+ * commit's number.
+ */
+static int omacvm_hdr_on = -1;          /* QEMU thread: -1 not read yet, 0 off or failed */
+static int omacvm_hdr_rule_c = -1;      /* qatomic: macOS 26+ and not OMACVM_HDR_SDR_TAG=0 */
+static int omacvm_hdr_trace;            /* qatomic: OMACVM_HDR_TRACE=1 */
+static int omacvm_hdr_need_c = 100;     /* qatomic: 100 = PQ frames SDR (no EDR), 0 = HDR */
+static int64_t omacvm_hdr_open_ns = -1; /* qatomic: when PQ frames last turned HDR */
+static unsigned omacvm_hdr_commit_seq;  /* qatomic: commits counted for the trace */
+static __thread unsigned omacvm_hdr_commit_now; /* this thread's commit (trace) */
+static int omacvm_hdr_display_gen;      /* qatomic: the main thread saw another display */
+static struct {
+    OmacvmHdrNeed n;
+    bool active;                        /* the last frame drawn was PQ */
+    bool flagged_any;                   /* a surface ever had the SDR flag */
+    int display_gen;
+    int made;                           /* the peak program: 1 made, -1 failed */
+    GLuint prog, vao, vbo, fbo, tex[2], pbo;
+    GLint u_size;
+    int w, h, rw, rh;                   /* the frame size the targets are for; the last pass's */
+    bool pending;                       /* a read back waits for the timer */
+    int64_t look_ns;
+    QEMUTimer *timer;
+} omacvm_hdr;
+
+static void omacvm_hdr_read(int64_t now, bool in_present);
+
+static void omacvm_hdr_timer_cb(void *opaque)
+{
+    omacvm_hdr_read(qemu_clock_get_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME), false);
+}
+
+/* Any thread: does the rule run here (macOS 26+, not OMACVM_HDR_SDR_TAG=0)? Read once. */
+static bool omacvm_hdr_rule(void)
+{
+    int r = qatomic_read(&omacvm_hdr_rule_c);
+
+    if (r < 0) {
+        NSOperatingSystemVersion v = [[NSProcessInfo processInfo] operatingSystemVersion];
+        r = omacvm_hdr_rule_on((int)v.majorVersion, getenv("OMACVM_HDR_SDR_TAG"));
+        qatomic_set(&omacvm_hdr_rule_c, r);
+    }
+    return r;
+}
+
+/* QEMU thread: the switches, read once. */
+static bool omacvm_hdr_wanted(void)
+{
+    if (omacvm_hdr_on < 0) {
+        const char *t = getenv("OMACVM_HDR_TRACE");
+        omacvm_hdr_on = omacvm_hdr_rule();
+        qatomic_set(&omacvm_hdr_trace, t && !strcmp(t, "1"));
+        if (!omacvm_hdr_on) {
+            qatomic_set(&omacvm_hdr_need_c, 0);
+            info_report("cocoa: HDR: EDR on for every PQ frame, as in 3.2.22 (%s)",
+                        omacvm_hdr_rule_on(99, getenv("OMACVM_HDR_SDR_TAG")) ?
+                        "macOS before 26: not checked there" : "OMACVM_HDR_SDR_TAG=0");
+        }
+        omacvm_hdr.timer = timer_new_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME, omacvm_hdr_timer_cb, NULL);
+    }
+    return omacvm_hdr_on == 1;
+}
+
+/* QEMU thread: the look cannot run: EDR on from now on, as before. */
+static void omacvm_hdr_fail(const char *why)
+{
+    omacvm_hdr_on = 0;
+    omacvm_hdr.made = -1;
+    omacvm_hdr.pending = false;
+    qatomic_set(&omacvm_hdr_need_c, 0);
+    timer_del(omacvm_hdr.timer);
+    warn_report("cocoa: HDR: no peak look (%s), EDR on for PQ frames as before", why);
+}
+
+static GLuint omacvm_hdr_shader(GLenum type, const char *src)
+{
+    GLuint s = glCreateShader(type);
+    GLint ok = 0;
+
+    glShaderSource(s, 1, &src, NULL);
+    glCompileShader(s);
+    glGetShaderiv(s, GL_COMPILE_STATUS, &ok);
+    if (!ok) {
+        char why[512] = "";
+        glGetShaderInfoLog(s, sizeof(why), NULL, why);
+        warn_report("cocoa: HDR: the peak %s shader does not compile: %s",
+                    type == GL_VERTEX_SHADER ? "vertex" : "fragment", why);
+        glDeleteShader(s);
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return s;
+}
+
+/* QEMU thread, present_ctx current: the peak program, made once. */
+static bool omacvm_hdr_program(void)
+{
+    static const GLfloat quad[] = { -1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1 };
+
+    if (omacvm_hdr.made) {
+        return omacvm_hdr.made > 0;
+    }
+    GLuint vs = omacvm_hdr_shader(GL_VERTEX_SHADER, OMACVM_HDR_PEAK_VERT);
+    GLuint fs = omacvm_hdr_shader(GL_FRAGMENT_SHADER, OMACVM_HDR_PEAK_FRAG);
+    GLint ok = 0;
+    if (vs && fs) {
+        omacvm_hdr.prog = glCreateProgram();
+        glAttachShader(omacvm_hdr.prog, vs);
+        glAttachShader(omacvm_hdr.prog, fs);
+        glBindAttribLocation(omacvm_hdr.prog, 0, "in_position");
+        glLinkProgram(omacvm_hdr.prog);
+        glGetProgramiv(omacvm_hdr.prog, GL_LINK_STATUS, &ok);
+    }
+    glDeleteShader(vs);
+    glDeleteShader(fs);
+    if (!ok) {
+        if (omacvm_hdr.prog) {
+            glDeleteProgram(omacvm_hdr.prog);
+            omacvm_hdr.prog = 0;
+        }
+        omacvm_hdr.made = -1;
+        return false;
+    }
+    glUseProgram(omacvm_hdr.prog);
+    glUniform1i(glGetUniformLocation(omacvm_hdr.prog, "image"), 0);
+    omacvm_hdr.u_size = glGetUniformLocation(omacvm_hdr.prog, "size");
+    glUseProgram(0);
+    glGenVertexArrays(1, &omacvm_hdr.vao);
+    glBindVertexArray(omacvm_hdr.vao);
+    glGenBuffers(1, &omacvm_hdr.vbo);
+    glBindBuffer(GL_ARRAY_BUFFER, omacvm_hdr.vbo);
+    glBufferData(GL_ARRAY_BUFFER, sizeof(quad), quad, GL_STATIC_DRAW);
+    glVertexAttribPointer(0, 2, GL_FLOAT, GL_FALSE, 0, 0);
+    glEnableVertexAttribArray(0);
+    glBindBuffer(GL_ARRAY_BUFFER, 0);
+    glBindVertexArray(0);
+    glGenFramebuffers(1, &omacvm_hdr.fbo);
+    glGenBuffers(1, &omacvm_hdr.pbo);
+    glGenTextures(2, omacvm_hdr.tex);
+    omacvm_hdr.made = 1;
+    return true;
+}
+
+/* QEMU thread, present_ctx current: the passes' R32F targets for a w x h frame. */
+static bool omacvm_hdr_targets(int w, int h)
+{
+    if (w == omacvm_hdr.w && h == omacvm_hdr.h) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    int w1 = omacvm_hdr_blocks(w), h1 = omacvm_hdr_blocks(h);
+    int w2 = omacvm_hdr_blocks(w1), h2 = omacvm_hdr_blocks(h1);
+    bool ok = true;
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, omacvm_hdr.fbo);
+    for (int k = 0; k < 2; k++) {
+        glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, omacvm_hdr.tex[k]);
+        glTexImage2D(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, GL_R32F, k ? w2 : w1, k ? h2 : h1, 0,
+                     GL_RED, GL_FLOAT, NULL);
+        /* no mipmaps: complete (readable) only without a mipmap filter */
+        glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+        glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+        glFramebufferTexture2D(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0, GL_TEXTURE_2D,
+                               omacvm_hdr.tex[k], 0);
+        ok = ok && glCheckFramebufferStatus(GL_FRAMEBUFFER) == GL_FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE;
+    }
+    glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0);
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
+    glBindBuffer(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, omacvm_hdr.pbo);
+    glBufferData(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, (GLsizeiptr)w2 * h2 * sizeof(float), NULL, GL_STREAM_READ);
+    glBindBuffer(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, 0);
+    if (!ok) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    omacvm_hdr.w = w;
+    omacvm_hdr.h = h;
+    omacvm_hdr.rw = w2;
+    omacvm_hdr.rh = h2;
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * QEMU thread, present_ctx current: the two passes over the guest's frame
+ * (every pixel, whatever part of it the present draws) and a read back
+ * into the buffer, read by the timer 125 ms later (no wait for the GPU).
+ */
+static void omacvm_hdr_look(GLuint src, uint32_t w, uint32_t h)
+{
+    int64_t now = qemu_clock_get_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME);
+    bool trace = qatomic_read(&omacvm_hdr_trace);
+
+    if (omacvm_hdr.pending || (!trace && now - omacvm_hdr.look_ns < OMACVM_HDR_LOOK_NS)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_hdr_program()) {
+        omacvm_hdr_fail("no shader");
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_hdr_targets(w, h)) {
+        omacvm_hdr_fail("no float target");
+        return;
+    }
+    int w1 = omacvm_hdr_blocks(w), h1 = omacvm_hdr_blocks(h);
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, omacvm_hdr.fbo);
+    glDisable(GL_BLEND);
+    glDisable(GL_SCISSOR_TEST);
+    glColorMask(GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE);
+    glUseProgram(omacvm_hdr.prog);
+    glBindVertexArray(omacvm_hdr.vao);
+    glActiveTexture(GL_TEXTURE0);
+    for (int k = 0; k < 2; k++) {
+        glFramebufferTexture2D(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0, GL_TEXTURE_2D,
+                               omacvm_hdr.tex[k], 0);
+        glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, k ? omacvm_hdr.tex[0] : src);
+        if (!k) {
+            /* texelFetch needs a complete texture; the present sets its own filter after */
+            glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+            glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+        }
+        glViewport(0, 0, k ? omacvm_hdr.rw : w1, k ? omacvm_hdr.rh : h1);
+        glUniform2i(omacvm_hdr.u_size, k ? w1 : (GLint)w, k ? h1 : (GLint)h);
+        glDrawArrays(GL_TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);
+    }
+    glBindBuffer(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, omacvm_hdr.pbo);
+    glReadPixels(0, 0, omacvm_hdr.rw, omacvm_hdr.rh, GL_RED, GL_FLOAT, 0);
+    glBindBuffer(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, 0);
+    glBindVertexArray(0);
+    glUseProgram(0);
+    glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0);
+    glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
+    omacvm_hdr.pending = true;
+    omacvm_hdr.look_ns = now;
+    if (trace) {
+        omacvm_hdr_read(now, true);
+    } else {
+        timer_mod(omacvm_hdr.timer, now + OMACVM_HDR_LOOK_NS / 2);
+    }
+}
+
+/* QEMU thread: SDR <-> HDR: a log line, and the newest frame again (a whole one). */
+static void omacvm_hdr_changed(int64_t now, bool redraw)
+{
+    bool one = omacvm_hdr.n.need > 0;
+
+    qatomic_set(&omacvm_hdr_need_c, one ? 100 : 0);
+    if (!one) {
+        qatomic_set(&omacvm_hdr_open_ns, now);
+    }
+    info_report(one ? "cocoa: HDR: SDR frames (peak %.2fx), EDR off" :
+                      "cocoa: HDR: HDR frames (peak %.2fx), EDR on",
+                omacvm_hdr.n.peak);
+    if (redraw) {
+        gl_dirty = true;
+        cocoa_gl_present_request();
+    }
 }
 
+/* QEMU thread (BQL): the look's result, then the rule; the timer for the hold. */
+static void omacvm_hdr_read(int64_t now, bool in_present)
+{
+    bool changed = false;
+
+    if (omacvm_hdr_on != 1) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (omacvm_hdr.pending) {
+        size_t n = (size_t)omacvm_hdr.rw * omacvm_hdr.rh;
+        CGLContextObj prev = CGLGetCurrentContext();
+        CGLSetCurrentContext(present_ctx);
+        glBindBuffer(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, omacvm_hdr.pbo);
+        const float *v = glMapBufferRange(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, 0, n * sizeof(float),
+                                          GL_MAP_READ_BIT);
+        double m = v ? omacvm_hdr_max(v, n) : NAN;
+        if (v) {
+            glUnmapBuffer(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER);
+        }
+        glBindBuffer(GL_PIXEL_PACK_BUFFER, 0);
+        CGLSetCurrentContext(prev);
+        omacvm_hdr.pending = false;
+        if (!v) {
+            omacvm_hdr_fail("the read back failed");
+            if (!in_present) {
+                gl_dirty = true;
+                cocoa_gl_present_request();
+            }
+            return;
+        }
+        double peak = omacvm_hdr_pq_units(m);
+        if (qatomic_read(&omacvm_hdr_trace)) {
+            info_report("cocoa: hdr-trace: frame peak code %ld (%.3fx)", lround(m * 1023), peak);
+        }
+        changed = omacvm_hdr_need_peak(&omacvm_hdr.n, peak, now);
+    }
+    changed |= omacvm_hdr_need_tick(&omacvm_hdr.n, now);
+    if (changed) {
+        omacvm_hdr_changed(now, !in_present);
+    }
+    int64_t due = omacvm_hdr_need_due(&omacvm_hdr.n);
+    if (due >= 0) {
+        timer_mod(omacvm_hdr.timer, due);
+    }
+}
+
 /*
+ * QEMU thread, present_ctx current, before a frame is drawn: pq = it goes
+ * into PQ surfaces. PQ frames start SDR, no EDR (the VM's start, extra
+ * brightness off, the output turning 10-bit, another display); then a look.
+ */
+static void omacvm_hdr_frame(GLuint src, uint32_t w, uint32_t h, bool pq)
+{
+    if (!omacvm_hdr_wanted()) {
+        return;
+    }
+    int gen = qatomic_read(&omacvm_hdr_display_gen);
+    if (pq && (!omacvm_hdr.active || gen != omacvm_hdr.display_gen)) {
+        bool was_one = qatomic_read(&omacvm_hdr_need_c) > 0;
+        omacvm_hdr_need_reset(&omacvm_hdr.n);
+        omacvm_hdr.pending = false;
+        omacvm_hdr.display_gen = gen;
+        timer_del(omacvm_hdr.timer);
+        qatomic_set(&omacvm_hdr_need_c, 100);
+        if (!omacvm_hdr.flagged_any || !was_one) {
+            info_report("cocoa: HDR: PQ frames without EDR until one shows HDR "
+                        "(a look at the brightest pixel 4 times a second)");
+        }
+    }
+    omacvm_hdr.active = pq;
+    if (pq && src) {
+        omacvm_hdr_look(src, w, h);
+    }
+}
+
+/*
+ * QEMU thread: a surface's SDR flag, before it goes to Core Animation: on
+ * a PQ surface whose frame is SDR, else none (EDR on, as before). Also
+ * taken off a surface that turned linear (extra brightness).
+ */
+static void omacvm_hdr_tag(IOSurfaceRef s)
+{
+    bool sdr = omacvm_hdr_on == 1 && present_deep && !present_linear && present_color == 1 &&
+               cocoa_gl_present_hdr_wanted() && qatomic_read(&omacvm_hdr_need_c) > 0;
+    if (!sdr && !omacvm_hdr.flagged_any) {
+        return;
+    }
+    CFTypeRef v = IOSurfaceCopyValue(s, CFSTR(OMACVM_HDR_SURF_SDR_KEY));
+    bool has = v != NULL;
+    if (v) {
+        CFRelease(v);
+    }
+    if (sdr && !has) {
+        IOSurfaceSetValue(s, CFSTR(OMACVM_HDR_SURF_SDR_KEY), kCFBooleanTrue);
+        omacvm_hdr.flagged_any = true;
+    } else if (!sdr && has) {
+        IOSurfaceRemoveValue(s, CFSTR(OMACVM_HDR_SURF_SDR_KEY));
+    }
+}
+
+/* Any thread: does the surface's frame show SDR only (its SDR flag)? */
+static bool omacvm_hdr_surf_sdr(IOSurfaceRef surf)
+{
+    CFTypeRef v = IOSurfaceCopyValue(surf, CFSTR(OMACVM_HDR_SURF_SDR_KEY));
+
+    if (v) {
+        CFRelease(v);
+    }
+    return v != NULL;
+}
+
+/* Any thread: a surface's headroom tag (extra brightness's 2.0), 0 without one. */
+static double omacvm_hdr_surf_tag(IOSurfaceRef surf)
+{
+    CFTypeRef v = IOSurfaceCopyValue(surf, kIOSurfaceContentHeadroom);
+    double d = 0;
+
+    if (v) {
+        if (CFGetTypeID(v) == CFNumberGetTypeID()) {
+            CFNumberGetValue((CFNumberRef)v, kCFNumberDoubleType, &d);
+        }
+        CFRelease(v);
+    }
+    return d;
+}
+
+/* Commit thread, in a transaction that shows a frame: its number for the trace. */
+static void omacvm_hdr_commit_begin(void)
+{
+    if (qatomic_read(&omacvm_hdr_trace)) {
+        omacvm_hdr_commit_now = qatomic_fetch_inc(&omacvm_hdr_commit_seq) + 1;
+    }
+}
+
+/* Commit thread, OMACVM_HDR_TRACE=1: what macOS is given for one layer. */
+static void omacvm_hdr_trace_layer(CALayer *layer, IOSurfaceRef surf)
+{
+    OSType f = IOSurfaceGetPixelFormat(surf);
+    char fs[5] = { (char)(f >> 24), (char)(f >> 16), (char)(f >> 8), (char)f, 0 };
+    CFTypeRef cs = IOSurfaceCopyValue(surf, kIOSurfaceColorSpace);
